WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.968
-My next guest is
a very talented director

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:06.539
whose latest film "In the
Heights" is now in theaters...

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:09.108
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:10.543
...and on HBO Max.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:14.146
Please welcome Jon M. Chu!

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:18.318
-♪ Meet a director,
don't know what to do ♪

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:22.588
♪ If you got dollars,
better hire Jon M. Chu ♪

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:26.358
♪ He did not do "Soul Plane,"
neither "Harlem Nights" ♪

00:00:26.358 --> 00:00:28.394
♪ But he did
"Crazy Rich Asians" ♪

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:30.930
♪ And he's here
for "In the Heights" ♪

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.131
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.200
-Oh, beautiful!

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.768
-The time has come.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:39.638
-The time has come!
It is. The time has come.

00:00:39.638 --> 00:00:41.741
Welcome, and thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.275
Standing ovation.
-Good to be here. I know.

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:45.444
The audience is here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:47.146
-Full audience.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:49.682
-Can I show my movie after this?
'Cause I just want to feel that.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.483
-Yeah, we're going
to screen the movie, yeah.

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:52.985
Thank you
for coming on the show.

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:56.155
We've talked on the phone
before.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:57.957
-[ Laughs ] Yes, we --

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.059
Lin was with you,
and we briefly chatted.

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.595
I was on the set,
and I had an embarrassing moment

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.664
that I need to say.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:07.099
We were talking, and I took --
We were talking,

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:08.300
and I was like,
"I'm with Jimmy Fallon.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.169
Oh, my gosh."
So I took a screen grab,

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:13.172
and it says, "Jon Chu has taken
a screen grab" on your phone.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:15.040
And I was like, "Oh, uh,

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.944
nice to meet you, Jimmy. Um..."

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:20.112
And then you handed the phone
off to Lin.

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:22.047
-Yeah, no, no.
-Was that okay?

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:23.850
-That was way okay.
It's more than okay.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.651
Yeah, I was so --
'cause I was with Lin,

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:30.222
and he was saying, like, he's
like, "Jon, Jon Chu is amazing.

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:33.459
He edits as he's --"
as you're doing it.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.228
'Cause this was --
This was a while back.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.196
-It was a while back.
-And it was --

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:39.899
And you edit while --
like right after you shoot?

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:42.335
-I mean, listen, I have
an editor, a great editor,

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.403
Myron Kerstein,
but I do a little rough --

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:45.771
just so I know I got the shots.

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:48.040
-And he showed me
the first opening scene,

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.776
and then we talked to you
on the FaceTime.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.611
And I was like,
it was just amazing.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.012
-Yes. You're being so nice,

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.814
and I was like [Imitates click]
"He took a screenshot."

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.250
-[ Laughs ] No. No, I mean,

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.118
I want to talk to you
about "In the Heights"

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.753
'cause it is so great.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.423
Congratulations. You really
did a great job with this.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.224
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:06.558
-What a big week for you,

00:02:06.558 --> 00:02:09.595
because not only is
"In the Heights" out right now,

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.764
but also, your wife
is expecting a baby

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.232
literally any second.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.034
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.070
-I know. Get your phone out.
-Got to make sure.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.438
-Make sure
your phone's on, yeah.

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.139
-I was leaving. I was like,
"I'm going to my premiere.

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:21.441
Can you, like, not have a baby?"

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:24.210
I was -- "Keep your legs tight."

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.579
I googled. I literally googled

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.848
"What not to do
to not have a baby."

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.250
So I --
-Really?

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.251
-No shampoo. No shampoo.
-Is that right?

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:33.853
-I guess there's a smell
triggers something.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.288
-Yeah. But it's really --
It might happen any --

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:39.091
-Literally. I'm going
to keep this here for real.

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:42.462
-Oh, my gosh. I'm so excited.
That's fantastic news.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.563
What was it like last night?

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:45.931
What was it like
in Washington Heights?

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:47.833
-Oh, man. It felt -- I mean,
to hear this audience,

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:50.202
it felt very similar,
just in a larger space

00:02:50.202 --> 00:02:51.971
and to have -- to show
in Washington Heights,

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.205
where the songs were inspired --

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:57.076
You know, Lin-Manuel Miranda
wrote these songs.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.144
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.045
-Oh, he's unbelievable.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.946
-And to return to his hometown

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:02.648
to show the movie
where we shot it?

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:04.183
That audience went nuts.

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:05.885
You could feel the energy, so...
-You could, right?

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.953
-Yeah. I mean, that's why
it says the time has come.

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:09.555
The time has come
that people are coming out

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:12.124
and joining hands again to know
you can get back up out of this.

00:03:12.124 --> 00:03:13.626
So...
-Yeah. And it's --

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:14.727
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.962
You can.
-Yeah.

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:21.066
-How important was it for you to
have the movie play in theaters?

00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:23.936
-Super important. I mean, I went
through "Crazy Rich Asians"

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:26.706
a couple years back. Yeah, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.174
-Not too shabby.

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.909
-But what I love about it,
and it was that it's the stars,

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:32.779
these actors who never had
these opportunities,

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.847
got to be on the cover
of magazines,

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.883
got to be here on your couch,
Henry Golding,

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.351
which, thank you for that.
-He's the best.

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:41.587
-And hosting "SNL."

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:43.722
I mean, they are now
creating a path for them.

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:45.091
And for "In the Heights,"
I was like,

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.660
"We need the marketing
department of Warner Bros.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.462
to, like, go and spend money
on these people,"

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.965
to show that the people
of Washington Heights, that --

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:56.535
you know, Latinos
only get 4.5% of talking,

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:58.070
of dialogue in movies,

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.207
and they make up
over 40% of the audience.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.409
And so we need to say
we want more of this.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.378
And so the fact that -- Yeah.

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.746
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:10.683
And the box office
is one of the only places

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.184
that the audience can say,

00:04:12.184 --> 00:04:14.586
"We want this. I don't care
about your precedent.

00:04:14.586 --> 00:04:17.590
I don't care what your --
what you think in a boardroom.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.992
We want it," and they will
give it to you, I promise you.

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.394
So, yeah, it's great.
-Well, this was clearly --

00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:26.832
I was saying backstage the movie
is made clearly with love

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:28.901
and you could feel it,
and it is emotion,

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.235
and the story is so great.

00:04:30.235 --> 00:04:33.506
You did such an amazing job
capturing New York City

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.241
and how hot it is in the summer.

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.776
And -- No, it is something
about that,

00:04:37.776 --> 00:04:40.379
and it's something
that we all can relate to

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:42.382
when it's just a hot day,
and you're like, "I'm just --

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.883
Anything," like Piragua Guy.

00:04:44.883 --> 00:04:47.219
You want anything. You want
to put the hose on you.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:48.221
It doesn't matter.
-Yeah.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.889
-And then, also, it's like,

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:51.457
don't forget
where you came from,

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.425
and don't forget
to keep dreaming,

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:54.594
and what is the dream?

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.162
-Yeah, that's why we connected,
Lin and I.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.997
It was like we knew what --
I'm from Northern California.

00:04:58.997 --> 00:05:00.399
I grew up
in a Chinese restaurant

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.901
that my dad has for 51 years,
still open --

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:04.069
Chef Chu's in California.

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:06.238
And --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:07.740
I got to plug it.
I got to plug it.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.709
-And -- And I knew what it
felt like to grow up there,

00:05:10.709 --> 00:05:12.678
to be raised
by not just your parents,

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:13.979
but your aunties and your uncles

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:17.149
and to hardworking people
who take care of their families.

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:18.818
And we should be looking up
to these people.

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.688
That bodega owner on the corner,
he does not have a small store.

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:23.556
He has a dream
bigger than any screen

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:25.124
that you can
put in front of him.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:26.359
He has hopes and dreams.

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:28.360
And to me,
that's what movies can do.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.862
That's what movies can can say.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.931
And if we see it,
you can't un-see that.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:35.601
-Yeah. And it was --

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.837
Was it -- You shot
in the neighborhood.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.006
-Yeah. Oh, yeah.
-In Washington Heights.

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:42.474
-It was awesome.
They really welcome you there.

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:44.510
They yell at you
if you're in their parking spot.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.812
-Of course. It's New York City.

00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:49.782
-Yeah. And they don't care
about a cone in the street.

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.617
They'll just drive right there.
-Yeah!

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.952
-But they took care of me.
I put my mom on on the stoop.

00:05:53.952 --> 00:05:55.354
And I was like,
"Mom, do not move.

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:57.223
I've got to direct
this musical sequence."

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:59.024
And we do it,
and I come back, she's gone,

00:05:59.024 --> 00:06:00.093
and she's on the second floor

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.426
with a family
who's invited her up,

00:06:01.426 --> 00:06:03.629
and they're drinking beers,
hanging out the window.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:05.063
"Hey, good job!"

00:06:05.063 --> 00:06:07.133
Like, "Mom? Oh, gosh."

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.535
-I love that. You brought a clip

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.471
which just shows
exactly what I was saying

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:14.307
I think earlier,
like how much love everyone --

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:16.375
what a team,
what a crew, what --

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:19.011
Everybody top to bottom
wanted this thing to work.

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:21.447
When you yell cut,
they continued to celebrate.

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:22.715
-Yeah.
-And dance.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.216
And that's when you know,
it's like, "Wow,

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:26.319
we're actually making something
out of love, and it's fun."

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:27.953
I want to show this footage
that you brought us.

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:29.155
Check this out.

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.524
[ Crowd cheering, chanting ]

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.672
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:48.574
That's not even in the movie.
-Come on.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:50.743
-That's not even in the movie.
That's just people loving.

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:52.511
-I literally called, "Cut,"
and they just kept going.

00:06:52.511 --> 00:06:54.680
And then people who were there
in the neighborhood

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.181
are hanging out the window
with their flags,

00:06:56.181 --> 00:06:57.450
and they're so proud.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.418
And then Lin is standing
up there on the fire escape,

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:02.054
and they all look up at Lin,
and they start chanting, "Lin,

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:04.523
Lin, Lin, Lin,"
all the crew members.

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:07.559
"Lin, Lin." I'm out there.
Because he manifested this.

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:08.894
He didn't have a role
for himself,

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:10.262
so he wrote a role for himself.

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:12.164
His community didn't have
a role, so he wrote this.

00:07:12.164 --> 00:07:14.700
And now a decade later,
more than a decade later,

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.103
they're here in front of him
making a movie.

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:19.304
And they all know
that big dreams can happen.

00:07:19.304 --> 00:07:20.540
They're all going to take that
for the rest --

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.174
I'm going to take that
for the rest of my life.

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:23.809
-I love it.

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:26.545
I want to show everyone a clip
from "In the Heights,"

00:07:26.545 --> 00:07:27.980
which is out now!

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.949
Take a look at this. Go see it.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:31.950
-[ Rapping ]
♪ Here goes Mr. Braggadocio ♪

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.720
♪ Next thing you know,
you lyin' like Pinocchio ♪

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:37.355
-♪ Yo, if you scared of
the bull, stay out the rodeo ♪

00:07:37.355 --> 00:07:40.459
-♪ Yo, I got more flows
than Obi-Wan Kenobi, oh ♪

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:42.929
-♪ Oh, you better stop rappin',
you not ready ♪

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:45.731
♪ It's gonna get hot and heavy,
and you already sweaty ♪

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:46.999
-♪ Yo, yo, yo ♪
-♪ Yo, yo ♪

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.634
♪ I'm sorry,
was that an answer? ♪

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:51.703
♪ Shut up, go home,
and pull your damn pants up ♪

00:07:51.703 --> 00:07:54.106
♪ As for you,
Mr. Frodo of the Shire ♪

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.308
-What?
-♪ 96 G's ♪

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:57.342
♪ Ain't enough to retire ♪
Come on!

00:07:57.342 --> 00:07:59.745
-♪ I'll have enough
to knock your ass off its axis ♪

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:03.449
-♪ You'll have a knapsack
full of jack after taxes ♪

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:05.084
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:06.852
-Anthony Ramos.
-Anthony Ramos.

00:08:06.852 --> 00:08:08.420
-Anthony Ramos, I mean --
-That kid.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.055
-Everything was fantastic.

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:11.390
Jon M. Chu, everybody.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:13.025
"In the Heights" is in theaters!

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:15.628
Go to the theaters!

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:17.362
Did we get anything,
any messages from the wife?

00:08:17.362 --> 00:08:18.865
We're all good.
Give her my love.

